Subject: [PATCH 102/159] [ae-patch] Group sidebar sessions by triage status
 and order them by hand

Reid asked on 2026-10-18 to sort sessions by drag and drop or a chosen order,
to group them by status with visual separation, and to choose between
automatic grouping and a fully manual order. This builds on upstream's
sidebar_grouping_ui view options (2026-10-19) rather than a parallel view.

Grouping gains Triage: Pinned on top, then Blocked, Working, Review, No
status, Parked and Reference, each header showing the status glyph, the word
and a row count, then an Archived group that stays collapsed and loads
archived sessions only once opened. A row's group holds while the pointer is
in the list, like the Status grouping.

Ordering gains Manual: one saved order per user (GET and PUT /v1/ae/sidebar,
served out of tree) ranks Sessions, Shared, each project folder and each
group. Sessions missing from it sort on top, so new ones land first, and a
move changes only the moved row. Rows move by drag within their own list and
through a Move submenu in the row menu (flat items on a phone). Moves show at
once and save in turn on the latest order; a save the server refuses as stale
replays once on the order it returned. Manual is off while searching and on
the Archived display. Triage and Manual load list pages up to the 100 rows
the background refresh keeps current.

A drop on a row-order target is always consumed, since upstream reads an
unknown drop target as the Sessions list and would unfile a session dropped
on a sibling in its own folder. Settings > Chat gains a Session list row with
a reset of the manual order and an Undo.

The logic lives in new AE files; Sidebar.tsx gets small hunks at the edit
sites (view labels, the group order and titles, the order applied to the
lists, the drop guard, the collision filter, an optional header title node,
the Move menu, the row drop target and the Archived group).
